res_query failed every query with NO_RECOVERY, so that mtr found no
network's AS number (its -z and -y ask origin.asn.cymru.com's TXT
records), and res_init and its kin said they were stubs on standard
error, in the middle of mtr's screen. res_query now asks the
nameservers of /etc/resolv.conf with the lookups' own queries, for any
type and class, without the search list, as glibc does: it gives the
answer, cut to the buffer with TC set when it does not fit, or -1 with
h_errno HOST_NOT_FOUND, NO_DATA, TRY_AGAIN or NO_RECOVERY as glibc's
would. res_init, res_ninit and res_nclose say nothing, as each query
reads /etc/resolv.conf (ADR 0345).
Meant for upstream.

